# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this file the checked-in line endings depend on each machine's
# core.autocrlf, and the repository already drifted: most files were LF while a
# handful of Markdown and Python files were committed with CRLF. Every added line
# in those files then carried a trailing \r, which `git diff --check` reports as
# trailing whitespace, making the validation step in docs/repository-policy.md
# impossible to pass.
#
# text=auto still detects binary content by itself, so no per-extension rules are
# needed for the files this repository holds today.
* text=auto eol=lf
